* @title Unevaluated expression uses current word in a prebuilt pattern
* @attribution Griswold 1971, Chapter 2, Section 2.16
* @input >>>
* THESE TWO STRINGS ARE ALMOST ALIKE.
* THE TWO STRINGS AREN'T ALIKE.
* <<<
* @expect >>>
* TWO, STRINGS, ALIKE,
* <<<
          &ANCHOR = 0; &TRIM = 1
          WORD = BREAK(' .,') . W SPAN(' .,')
          FINDW = ' ' *W ANY(' .,')
          STRING1 = INPUT ' ' :F(ERROR)
          STRING2 = ' ' INPUT ' ' :F(ERROR)
LOOP      STRING1 WORD = :F(OUTPUT)
          STRING2 FINDW :F(LOOP)
          LIST = LIST W ', ' :(LOOP)
OUTPUT    OUTPUT = TRIM(LIST)
END
